# Player profiles and player cards

Two new pages for logged-in players. Tests before code (AGENTS.md).

## Decisions

1. Achievements: games post unlocks to the server (`POST /api/achievements`).
2. Profile picture: user uploads a file or picks a preset (both). Server re-encodes with Pillow
   to a 256 px square, stored under `DATA_DIR/avatars/`.
3. Wish list: rich text with links. Create a link with Ctrl-K (Cmd-K on Mac), or select text and
   right-click, like Teams, Word and PowerPoint.
4. Editing: the owner and admins (`ADMINS`) can edit a profile.
5. Player cards: all logged-in players see all cards. Each card shows scores and achievement
   badges. Nav link `/spillere`.
6. Persistence: deferred. Decide later how `DATA_DIR` is kept on Render.

## Open questions

A. Achievements (agreed: 1a, a POST endpoint that games call).

   Tracks and tiers:
   - Each game defines at most 3 tracks. A track is one kind of achievement (e.g. gifts collected).
   - Each track has tiers in increasing order (e.g. 1 present, 10 presents, 25 presents).
   - A higher tier replaces the lower tier on the card. Only the highest reached tier per track is
     shown, so a card never has more than 3 badges per game.
   - Achievement id format: `<game>:<track>:<tier>`, e.g. `snake:gifts:10`.

   API: `POST /api/achievements` with `{achievement_id}`. The server stores the unlock for the
   session user and ignores repeats. The server does not decide tiers; games send the tier they reached.

   Snake tracks (proposed, 3 max; gifts track dropped, it correlates with score):
   - `snake:ghost-cross`: cross your own body while ghosting (see below). Tiers TBD.
   - Two more tracks TBD. Candidates from the existing code: shield saves (`snake:shield`),
     save streak (`snake:lives`). Pick the two to keep, with their tiers.

   Ghost loops (agreed rules):
   - Ghost gives 10 ticks of passing through the body (GHOST_TICKS = 10).
   - A loop is recorded when the head moves into a body cell while ghosting and stays alive.
   - After a loop, the next floor item is always a ghost powerup.
   - The card text hints at coiling without naming the mechanic (done, commit b38aea8).

   Loop tiers (agreed names):
   - Tier 1, one loop: Nidhogg.
   - Tier 2, two loops at once: Ouroboros.
   - Tier 3, three loops at once: Jormungandr (spelling Jörmungandr if the card font supports it).

   Snake tracks (3 max per game). Agreed:
   - Loops: Nidhogg, Ouroboros, Jormungandr (see above).
   - `snake:shield`: most shields held at once. Proposed 5, 10, 20.
   - `snake:trim`: trim pickups in one run. Proposed 5, 10, 20.
   Measured with the game's rules (2000 simulated runs, simple bot, 20x20 board):
   - Most shields held at once: best run 6. 5 reached by 1.7% of runs; 10 and 20 never.
   - Trims in one run: best run 8. 5 reached by 1.9% of runs; 10 and 20 never.
   Open: 10 and 20 are unreachable with the current spawn rates. Options: lower thresholds,
   or raise the shield/trim share of spawns, or keep them as aspirational tiers.
   Trim rule: removes 3 tail segments, never below 5 segments. Score is kept.

   Badges show the name on hover (title) and the snark as tooltip text.

   Existing unlocks: left in localStorage, not migrated (agreed: 2).

B. Wish list storage (agreed: sanitized HTML, allowlisted tags and URL schemes).
   Options considered: Options:
   - a. Store sanitized HTML. Allowlist tags (`a`, `b`, `i`, `u`, `br`, `ul`, `ol`, `li`) and
     `href` schemes (`https`, `http`, `mailto`) in Python with `html.parser`, no new dependency.
   - b. Store Markdown, render with the existing escape helper. Simpler and safer, but users
     don't get Word-style formatting.
   Recommended: a, because the editor is contenteditable and the sanitizer is the trust boundary.

## Data

- `profiles(name PK, wish_html TEXT, avatar_path TEXT, updated_at TEXT)`
- `achievements(name, achievement_id, unlocked_at, PK(name, achievement_id))`

## API

- `GET /api/profile/{name}`: public to logged-in users.
- `PUT /api/profile/{name}`: owner or admin. Wish length capped (4000 chars).
- `POST /api/profile/{name}/avatar`: multipart. Only JPEG/PNG/WebP, max 2 MB. Pillow re-encode
  to 256x256. Reject files that do not decode.
- `GET /api/players`: all players with profile, best score per game, achievements.
- `POST /api/achievements`: body `{achievement_id}`; caller is the session user only.

## Pages

- `/profil`: avatar (upload or preset picker), wish list editor with Ctrl-K link dialog.
- `/spillere`: grid of player cards. Mobile first, one column, then 2 and 3.
  Badges wrap and are never hidden by crowding. Scores show top 3 per game.

## Test plan (write first)

- Wish sanitizer: `<script>`, `javascript:` hrefs and `onerror` are removed; `https` links survive.
- Avatar: non-image rejected; oversize rejected; output is 256x256.
- Permissions: a non-owner non-admin gets 403 on PUT.
- Achievements POST is idempotent and only writes to the session user.
- `/spillere` renders a card per player with the user's badges.
- Playwright screenshots at phone and desktop widths.

